	(text "HP-SDI12-NANO r2 / COMPACT FLAT   -   11.5-14.4 V battery supply over the 3-wire SDI-12 cable. J1 has three bare cable solder holes (VIN,\ndata, ground); no connector is fitted. Asleep the board draws only the regulator (2.5 uA) plus MCU standby current."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 30 28.4 0)
		(effects (font (size 2 2)) (justify left bottom))
		(uuid "fadca3ca-9cc3-4dc4-9ae0-7940103b4880")
	)
	(text "SDI-12 DATA   -   meets the SDI-12 electrical numbers: R3 sets the 1-2 k\ntransmit resistance (and limits fault current into pin D2), R4 the\n160-360 k idle resistance, C4 holds the edge rate under 1.5 V/us. D4\nclamps cable transients."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 285 32.2 0)
		(effects (font (size 2 2)) (justify left bottom))
		(uuid "7d2d23e1-e965-466e-a0a4-8b5a59f68e4f")
	)
	(text "MICROCONTROLLER   -   Renesas RA4M1 (R7FA4M1AB3CFM), the Arduino UNO R4 / Nano R4 chip, wired exactly like the UNO R4 Minima so the stock\nboard package and Arduino pin names apply (nets D2, D4, D9, A0-A5). Runs at 5 V. Support circuit (NMI, USB sense, VCC_USB, VCL) follows\nArduino's Nano R4 schematic."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 30 124.8 0)
		(effects (font (size 2 2)) (justify left bottom))
		(uuid "76d0a838-f9cd-49f8-9150-319607c496a0")
	)
	(text "FIRMWARE ACCESS (no soldering)   -   J2 is a row of five holes for an off-the-shelf 2.54 mm 5-pin pogo clip. Holes 1-4 carry USB (5V, D-, D+,\nGND): plug a 'USB to 4-pin Dupont' cable onto the clip and the board is an 'Arduino UNO R4 Minima' in the IDE. Hole 5 = BOOT: only for the\nvery first load of the Arduino bootloader, put a jumper cap across clip pins 4-5 while plugging in. J5 = a second five-hole row (GND, 5V,\nSWDIO, SWCLK, RESET) for a debug probe if a board ever needs recovery."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 30 320.2 0)
		(effects (font (size 2 2)) (justify left bottom))
		(uuid "b308b790-3df5-4244-b453-ad3fb1768421")
	)
	(text "HEATER DRIVE + POWER MONITOR   -   PWM-capable D9/P303 drives Q1. Required\nfirmware: 100 Hz, nominal 2 W average, 8-15 s; integrate stable ON power times\nactual ON time. Force D9 LOW at shutdown; stopping a timer is insufficient. R10\npulls an undriven gate LOW. Keep all three INA226 inputs on their dedicated\nKelvin connections. Firmware is not included."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 430 23.6 0)
		(effects (font (size 2 2)) (justify left bottom))
		(uuid "1bcce54d-4ad3-450e-a374-3ff492cedc65")
	)
	(text "HEATER RESISTOR CHAIN (top of centre prong)   -   17 x 3.3 ohm 1% 0603 in series, 2.6 mm pitch. EXACT Vishay CRCW06033R30FKEAHP, 0.33 W at 70 C; no ordinary 0.1 W substitutes. Return is on bottom copper. Nominal full-ON power 2.34 W at 12 V, 3.41 W at 14.4 V with specified cable losses. PWM\ncontrols average energy; instantaneous ratings still apply. Qualify the potted needle thermally."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 30 368.4 0)
		(effects (font (size 2 2)) (justify left bottom))
		(uuid "8ecef694-624e-4406-ae3c-782f32ac4862")
	)
	(text "THERMISTORS   -   required firmware: 14-bit ADC, external VREF (AR_EXTERNAL), 64\nreadings averaged; actual noise and accuracy require measurement. The dividers\nand ADC reference share VREF. D4 switches thermistor ground through Q2 to reduce\nself-heating. Sequence: D4 HIGH, wait 10 ms, read, D4 LOW. R_ntc = Rref * code /\n(full scale - code). NTC = Murata NCP15XH103F03RC (10k, 1%); Rref = 10k 0.1% 25\nppm."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 430 177 0)
		(effects (font (size 2 2)) (justify left bottom))
		(uuid "878ea7c0-42d1-4a46-9a89-2ea9fdd23a47")
	)
